id: super-heavy
name: Super Heavy
kind: crafting
types: physical
slots: 1
# "Your ARC decides when this occurs": a switch on the Item, for when they have.
toggle: Accustomed
special: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Special. Attacks with it 2(bT) lower on the Strike Roll - until accustomed - and 5(bT) higher
  on the Wound Roll. Hardness Rank 4.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: Reduce your Strike Rolls with this Weapon by 2(bT), but increase your Wound Rolls
  by 5(bT). The Hardness Value for this Weapon is 4.

  [Passive]: While using this Weapon over time, you can become accustomed to the intense weight.
  Your ARC decides when this occurs, but when it does, remove the reduction to your Strike Rolls
  while using this Weapon.
text: >
  Super Heavy: This Weapon is weighted poorly, but the weight helps build your strength.
  –Weapon Type: Physical
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: Reduce your Strike Rolls with this Weapon by 2(bT), but increase your Wound Rolls by
  5(bT). The Hardness Value for this Weapon is 4.

  While using this Weapon over time, you can become accustomed to the intense weight. Your ARC
  decides when this occurs, but when it does, remove the reduction to your Strike Rolls while
  using this Weapon.

---

# The Strike's line alone goes once the switch is on: "remove the reduction to your Strike Rolls".
# The Wound Rolls are read as the Strike's are, with this Weapon. "The Hardness Value for this
# Weapon is 4" is its Hardness Rank, by the table's ruling - the Value is the Rank's.
[passive]
weapon.strike -= 2(bT); # until switched on
weapon.wound += 5(bT);
weapon.hardnessRank = 4;
